    "q-103236": {
      "dom_id": "step-q103236",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Using the extended Euclidean algorithm, compute integers $u$ and $v$ such that $80u+35v=\\text{gcd}(80,35).$ What is the value of $u+v?$",
      "worked_solution": "We will use the extended Euclidean algorithm. First, we apply the forward reduction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}80 & = & 35\\cdot 2 & + & 10 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 35 & = & 10\\cdot 3 & + & 5 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 10 & = & 5\\cdot 2 & + & 0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $\\text{gcd}(80,35)=5.$\n\nSolving for the remainders (the rightmost terms) in the equations above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10 & =80-35\\cdot 2 \\\\ 5 & =35-10\\cdot 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we back-substitute:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 & =35-10\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =35-[80-35\\cdot 2]\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =35\\cdot 7-80\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =80\\cdot (-3)+35\\cdot 7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $u=-3$ and $v=7.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\nu+v=(-3)+7=4.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
