    "q-78470": {
      "dom_id": "step-q78470",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Using the extended Euclidean algorithm, compute integers $u$ and $v$ such that $28u+16v=\\text{gcd}(28,16).$ What is the value of $u+v?$",
      "worked_solution": "We will use the extended Euclidean algorithm. First, we apply the forward reduction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}28 & = & 16\\cdot 1 & + & 12 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 16 & = & 12\\cdot 1 & + & 4 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 12 & = & 4\\cdot 3 & + & 0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $\\text{gcd}(16,28)=4.$\n\nSolving for the remainders (the rightmost terms) in the equations above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12 & =28-16 \\\\ 4 & =16-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we back-substitute:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =16-12 \\\\  & =16-(28-16) \\\\  & =16\\cdot 2-28 \\\\  & =28\\cdot (-1)+16\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $u=-1$ and $v=2.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\nu+v=(-1)+2=1.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-78470-a",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "-1",
              "html": "<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"45\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2212\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>"
            },
            {
              "option": "b",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-78470-b",
