    "q-76861": {
      "dom_id": "step-q76861",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Using the extended Euclidean algorithm, compute integers $u$ and $v$ such that $43u+17v=\\text{gcd}(43,17).$ What is the value of $u+v?$",
      "worked_solution": "We will use the extended Euclidean algorithm. First, we apply the forward reduction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}43 & = & 17\\cdot 2 & + & 9 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 17 & = & 9\\cdot 1 & + & 8 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 9 & = & 8\\cdot 1 & + & 1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $\\text{gcd}(17,43)=1.$\n\nSolving for the remainders (the rightmost terms) in the equations above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9 & =43-17\\cdot 2 \\\\ 8 & =17-9 \\\\ 1 & =9-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we back-substitute:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =9-8 \\\\  & =9-(17-9) \\\\  & =9\\cdot 2-17 \\\\  & =[43-17\\cdot 2]\\cdot 2-17 \\\\  & =43\\cdot 2-17\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =43\\cdot 2+17\\cdot (-5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $u=2$ and $v=-5.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\nu+v=2+(-5)=-3.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-76861-a",
