    "q-103265": {
      "dom_id": "step-q103265",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Using the extended Euclidean algorithm, compute integers $u$ and $v$ such that $55u+24v=\\text{gcd}(55,24).$ What is the value of $u+v?$",
      "worked_solution": "We will use the extended Euclidean algorithm. First, we apply the forward reduction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}55 & = & 24\\cdot 2 & + & 7 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 24 & = & 7\\cdot 3 & + & 3 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 7 & = & 3\\cdot 2 & + & 1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $\\text{gcd}(55,24)=1.$\n\nSolving for the remainders (the rightmost terms) in the equations above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7 & =55-24\\cdot 2 \\\\ 3 & =24-7\\cdot 3 \\\\ 1 & =7-3\\cdot 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we back-substitute:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =7-3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =7-[24-7\\cdot 3]\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =7\\cdot 7-24\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =[55-24\\cdot 2]\\cdot 7-24\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =55\\cdot 7-24\\cdot 16 \\\\  & =55\\cdot 7+24\\cdot (-16)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $u=7$ and $v=-16.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\nu+v=7+(-16)=-9.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
