    "q-79902": {
      "dom_id": "step-q79902",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Using the extended Euclidean algorithm, compute integers $u$ and $v$ such that $79u+35v=\\text{gcd}(79,35).$ What is the value of $u+v?$",
      "worked_solution": "We will use the extended Euclidean algorithm. First, we apply the forward reduction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}79 & = & 35\\cdot 2 & + & 9 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 35 & = & 9\\cdot 3 & + & 8 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 9 & = & 8\\cdot 1 & + & 1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $\\text{gcd}(79,35)=1.$\n\nSolving for the remainders (the rightmost terms) in the equations above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9 & =79-35\\cdot 2 \\\\ 8 & =35-9\\cdot 3 \\\\ 1 & =9-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we back-substitute:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =9-8 \\\\  & =9-[35-9\\cdot 3] \\\\  & =9\\cdot 4-35 \\\\  & =[79-35\\cdot 2]\\cdot 4-35 \\\\  & =79\\cdot 4-35\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =79\\cdot 4+35\\cdot (-9)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $u=4$ and $v=-9.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\nu+v=4+(-9)=-5.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
